{"id": "unknown-2026-10-27-030", "date": "2026-10-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 44, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["capacity"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["surpass"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.8, "reasons": ["情緒極端", "涉及產能"]}, "title": "Renewables to reach 40% of total generating capacity, beat gas within a year – EIA", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2025/09/Orsted-Revolution-Wind.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1200\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Over the coming year, renewables’ share of total generating capacity will grow from 37.7% to 40.4%, surpassing that of natural gas and outstripping nuclear capacity fivefold, according to new data released by the US Energy Information Administration (EIA) and reviewed by the SUN DAY Campaign.</p>\n\n\n\n <a da", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/10/27/renewables-to-reach-40-of-total-generating-capacity-beat-gas-within-a-year-eia/", "type": "rss"}]}
